# tally 2.2.1 P36 (L §6.1 l.1797, facts of movements stated same "read from both sides together, by every read"): N4, flows and
# count of either side of two movements stated same that disagree are HOLE-SAME, never one side's figure (review
# g2 min/b2 f1, f2; hs/h10). Before W8: 100.00 and 120.00 PLN, count 1 and 0.
=== h10.tally
model h10
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place wallet: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input d1: date
input d2: date
input a1: money PLN
input a2: money PLN
move in1: transfers
  on d1
  leg cash from world to wallet amount a1
move in2: transfers
  on d2
  leg cash from world to wallet amount a2
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  opening[wallet] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  d1 = 2026-03-05 "s"
  d2 = 2026-03-05 "s"
  a1 = 100.00 PLN "s"
  a2 = 120.00 PLN "s"
version later
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-05-01
  same in1 = in2
ask blc: bal(wallet, 2026-03-31)
ask blp: bal(wallet, 2026-03-31) with a2 = 100.00 PLN
ask bld: bal(wallet, 2026-03-31) with a2 = 100.00 PLN, d2 = 2026-03-09
ask f1: flows(in1, 2026-03)
ask f2: flows(in2, 2026-03)
ask f1p: flows(in1, 2026-03) with a2 = 100.00 PLN
ask f1q: flows(in1, 2026-03) with a2 = 130.00 PLN
ask f2d: flows(in2, 2026-03-05 .. 2026-03-05) with a2 = 100.00 PLN, d2 = 2026-03-09
ask fw: flows(wallet, 2026-03)
ask fwp: flows(wallet, 2026-03) with a2 = 100.00 PLN
ask sm0: sum(m.cash.amount for m in transfers over 2026-03)
ask sp: sum(m.cash.amount for m in transfers over 2026-03) with a2 = 100.00 PLN
ask sq: sum(m.cash.amount for m in transfers over 2026-03) with a2 = 130.00 PLN
ask c: count(m in transfers over 2026-03)
ask c5: count(m in transfers over 2026-03-05 .. 2026-03-05) with a2 = 100.00 PLN, d2 = 2026-03-09
ask c9: count(m in transfers over 2026-03-09 .. 2026-03-09) with a2 = 100.00 PLN, d2 = 2026-03-09
ask dp: m.day for m in transfers over 2026-03 with a2 = 100.00 PLN, d2 = 2026-03-05
ask x1: explain in1
ask x2: explain in2
ask ck: check (flows(in1, 2026-03)) == (flows(in2, 2026-03))
ask old: bal(wallet, 2026-03-31) as known 2026-04-01
=== expect f1 f2 f1p f1q f2d c c5 c9 ck
f1: ?"in1 and in2 are one, but the amount of cash differs on 2026-03-05: 100.00 PLN (in1) and 120.00 PLN (in2)" (in1, in2)
  unfulfilled: in1
  cut 2026-06-10
f2: ?"in1 and in2 are one, but the amount of cash differs on 2026-03-05: 100.00 PLN (in1) and 120.00 PLN (in2)" (in1, in2)
  unfulfilled: in2
  cut 2026-06-10
f1p: 100.00 PLN
  pinned: a2 = 100.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: in1
  cut 2026-06-10
f1q: ?"in1 and in2 are one, but the amount of cash differs on 2026-03-05: 100.00 PLN (in1) and 130.00 PLN (in2)" (in1, in2)
  pinned: a2 = 130.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: in1
  cut 2026-06-10
f2d: ?"in1 and in2 are one, but the day of cash differs on 2026-03-09: 2026-03-05 (in1) and 2026-03-09 (in2)" (in1, in2)
  cut 2026-06-10
c: 1
  unfulfilled: in1
  cut 2026-06-10
c5: ?"in1 and in2 are one, but the day of cash differs on 2026-03-05: 2026-03-05 (in1) and 2026-03-09 (in2)" (in1, in2)
  pinned: a2 = 100.00 PLN
  pinned: d2 = 2026-03-09
  unfulfilled: in1
  cut 2026-06-10
c9: ?"in1 and in2 are one, but the day of cash differs on 2026-03-05: 2026-03-05 (in1) and 2026-03-09 (in2)" (in1, in2)
  pinned: a2 = 100.00 PLN
  pinned: d2 = 2026-03-09
  unfulfilled: in1
  cut 2026-06-10
ck: (flows(in1, 2026-03)) = ?"in1 and in2 are one, but the amount of cash differs on 2026-03-05: 100.00 PLN (in1) and 120.00 PLN (in2)" (in1, in2), (flows(in2, 2026-03)) = ?"in1 and in2 are one, but the amount of cash differs on 2026-03-05: 100.00 PLN (in1) and 120.00 PLN (in2)" (in1, in2)
  unfulfilled: in1
  unfulfilled: in2
  cut 2026-06-10
